<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`pairLInsert` commutative).** Insertion of left children commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens, using commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`pairRInsert` commutative).** Insertion of right children commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens, using commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`atomInsert` commutative).** Insertion of atoms commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens, using commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`TreeToken`).** A tree token is bottom, an atom from the given domain, or a left or right child of a tree token.


**Definition (`instDecidableEqTreeToken`).** There is a type-class instance for decidable equality Tree Token.


**Definition (`atomInsert`).** The atom insertion adds the payload of the matching constructor and leaves every other constructor unchanged.


**Definition (`pairLInsert`).** The left-child insertion adds the payload of the matching constructor and leaves every other constructor unchanged.


**Definition (`pairLFinset`).** The set of left children.


**Theorem (`mem_foldr_pairL`).** A token lies in the fold of left children exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`mem_pairLFinset`).** A token lies in the mem set of left children exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`pairRInsert`).** The right-child insertion adds the payload of the matching constructor and leaves every other constructor unchanged.


**Definition (`pairRFinset`).** The set of right children.


**Theorem (`mem_foldr_pairR`).** A token lies in the fold of right children exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`mem_pairRFinset`).** A token lies in the mem set of right children exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`atomFinset`).** The atom finite set.


**Definition (`TreeCon`).** A finite set of tree tokens is consistent when every finite selection of atoms is consistent in $\mathbf{A}$ and the left and right children are themselves consistent.


**Theorem (`TreeCon.atom_con_of_atoms`).** The statement atom con of atoms holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`TreeCon.atoms_empty_of_right`).** The atoms empty of right of the empty set is empty.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`TreeCon.pairs_empty_of_left`).** The pairs empty of left of the empty set is empty.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`atomFinset_empty`).** The atom finite set empty of the empty set is empty.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`eq_singleton_bot_of_subset`).** The property eq singleton bot of subset passes to subsets.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`mem_foldr_atom`).** A token lies in the mem foldr atom exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`pairLFinset_empty`).** The set of left children empty of the empty set is empty.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`pairLFinset_insert_atom`).** Inserting the indicated constructor updates set of left children insert atom by adding that payload.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`pairLFinset_insert_bot`).** Inserting the indicated constructor updates set of left children insert bot by adding that payload.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`pairLFinset_insert_pairL`).** Inserting the indicated constructor updates set of left children insert pair L by adding that payload.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`pairLFinset_insert_pairR`).** Inserting the indicated constructor updates set of left children insert pair R by adding that payload.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`pairLFinset_mono`).** The operation set of left children mono preserves inclusion.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`pairLFinset_singleton_atom`).** On a singleton, set of left children singleton atom returns the payload of that one constructor.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


